node_modules/

# estimator.js used to be here. server.js now requires it AND serves it at
# /estimator.js, so ignoring it meant a deployed server that crashed on boot
# with MODULE_NOT_FOUND. A file the server requires is not local tooling.

# Local ingest and tooling — never deployed
ingest.js
sourcerank.js
jpreconcile.js

# yuyutei.js was here, on the same reasoning as the probes above: local
# tooling. That reasoning was "needs a database URL or a residential IP"
# and yuyu-tei needs NEITHER. Probed 2026-09-20 from both ends: 200 and
# 1,172,188 bytes from a home IP, the same 200 and the same 1,172,188
# bytes from Render. server.js now requires it to serve live Japanese
# listings.
#
# This is the estimator.js mistake, recorded at the top of this file: a
# file the server requires is not local tooling, and ignoring it means a
# deployed server that crashes on boot with MODULE_NOT_FOUND. The parser
# is SHARED with the local ingest rather than copied, because two
# implementations of one parser is how every other pair in this project
# drifted apart.
tcgdexprobe.js
tcgdexharvest.js
ebayprobe.js
yahoogate.js

# setaudit.js is DELIBERATELY TRACKED, unlike every probe above it.
# Those need a database URL or a residential IP; setaudit is read-only over
# the public API, so it runs from anywhere, including CI and another machine.
# It is the tool that proved the API was clean while the frontend was not, and
# that argument is only reproducible if the tool ships with the code.
#
# What actually keeps it tracked is that it IS tracked: .gitignore does not
# apply to files already in the index. This negation only helps against a
# sweeping pattern added ABOVE it -- git is last-match-wins, so a broad rule
# added further down still wins. Verified with `git check-ignore --no-index`,
# which is the form that ignores index state; without --no-index it reports
# a tracked file as unmatched and tells you nothing.
# setlist.test.js asserts the file is tracked, which is the durable guard.
!setaudit.js
gradeprices.js
*.test.js
jptest.js

